<title>FRANCE: French employers' chief seeks currency moderation.</title>
<headline>French employers' chief seeks currency moderation.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jean Gandois, head of France's employers' federation, the CNPF, said on Wednesday that countries which adopt the euro should ensure its credibility without trying to make it the &quot;world's strongest currency&quot;.</p>
<p>He told a meeting of corporate treasurers that Germany's belief that &quot;one must do everything to ensure that the currency be as strong as possible is not desirable&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;It's necessary to have a single currency which is sufficiently strong to be credible...but it should not always be aiming for maximum strength,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He added that he did not expect the single currency to be put into effect before its scheduled start-up date on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 wem/pmc</p>
